From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 01:52:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] j604: carry the J604 series onto integration/aurora
 abd6d4a09f

The J604 series was rebased from integration/aurora cc7696978e4c onto
abd6d4a09ffe, our side kept in every conflicting hunk. This commit
brings the result to the tree of the series merged with Aurora's tip,
where both sides changed the same code:

- Aurora's J604 pieces are carried and ours dropped: the Touch ID SPI
  mode, the SIO window at its mailbox and the AOP sensor services are
  Aurora's commits now. DisplayPort alt mode on the USB-C ports follows
  Aurora's design: the board marks the PHYs wired for it
  (apple,dp-alt-mode; ATC0, ATC1 and ATC3 on the J604), the display
  fabric routes alt mode only to those, a Type-C port's DP link rate
  runs Aurora's T8132 sequence with its T8132 lane start, and USB3+DP
  powers AUX up after the calibration. A Type-C port runs four DP lanes
  only where it is marked and calibrated.
- The HDMI port keeps the J604 series' DisplayPort-only PHY on ATC2 and
  its link rate path; it now takes Aurora's T8132 lane start too.
- The J604's speakers keep the J616s configuration (brought up, under
  speakersafetyd); Aurora's J604 entry kept them off.
- The video encoder takes Aurora's M4 Max and T6050 firmware
  identification next to the T8132 CRC; its MCTF and CMP420 code stays
  out, as in the series before.
- brcmfmac's reset keeps the J713 sleep ownership check and takes
  Aurora's link state.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
